# f1 = groupBy, f2 = single, f3 = isRecord, f4 = updated, f5 = written, f6 = asked
# For an update under a computed key the front end takes the key once: it tests it for an object, makes a property key of the object, and the access reads a parameter of the join behind. The scan
# did not see the call behind that parameter, so `(groups[name(row)] ??= []).push(row)` left the helper its rope (157,578 instructions a turn of the peer's 16-group-summary.mjs so written, against
# 65,567 with a read and a store). What is made a property key is read as a key: the conversion says it of the call whose answer it takes, straight (a computed member) or by the name that the test gave it.
# A call whose answer is only asked whether it is an object is told nothing.
# RUN: walk f4:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f4:Body
# CHECK: Strcat {{*}} [isLikelyKey]
# CHECK: Strcat {{*}} [isLikelyKey]
# RUN(WRITTEN): walk f5:Body mechanisms=all
# WRITTEN-LABEL: code f5:Body
# WRITTEN: Strcat {{*}} [isLikelyKey]
# RUN(ASKED): walk f6:Body mechanisms=all
# ASKED-LABEL: code f6:Body
# ASKED-NOT: isLikelyKey
